  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Startup events supporting the Tanzanian Business Angel Acceleration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the programme is to increase availability of local capital for Tanzania startups by building capacities of new angel investors and supporting them to join existing angel networks or set up generalist/sector-based angel networks based on their preferred investment strategies. Other objectives are:&#x2022;	To remove early-stage investment bottlenecks by creating Tanzania-centric angel investing resources and guidelines to help budding angel investors seamlessly kickstart successful investment activities in Tanzania&#x2022;	To increase quality startup pipelines that are investment ready, by developing Hub-Investor partnership framework to foster synergies between hubs and angel investors in delivering quality venture development programmes. &#x2022;	To increase the number of foreign investments attracted by Tanzania startups by increasing the number of local angel investment deals per year.This project (cohort 2) enables a large number of angel investors to cooperate on the common goal of strengthening local entrepreneurs by investing in sound startups. During the last year cohort 1 was already executed, financed by the United Nations Capital Development Fund (UNCDF).</narrative>
  </description>
